WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.719 --> 00:00:10.060
was getting ready for Christmas with her family.

2
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.262
She was stringing brightly colored beads with her brother, Danny.

3
00:00:14.282 --> 00:00:16.402
"Guess what?"

4
00:00:17.403 --> 00:00:20.384
Grandma called from the kitchen, where she was baking cookies.

5
00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:22.885
"It's snowing!"

6
00:00:26.646 --> 00:00:30.188
of delight came from the children as they raced to look out the window.

7
00:00:32.104 --> 00:00:35.026
"It's going to be a white Christmas after all!"

8
00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:36.067
cried Ella.

9
00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:39.209
"Hey, look who's here!"

10
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.011
said Danny, as Dad entered the room.

11
00:00:42.871 --> 00:00:45.153
He was covered with snow, holding up a tree.

12
00:00:45.173 --> 00:00:49.396
"Now who is going to help me decorate this?"

13
00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.297
Dad asked with a grin.

14
00:00:52.778 --> 00:00:57.341
Just then, Mom came downstairs carrying a big box of Christmas decorations.

15
00:00:57.361 --> 00:01:01.544
"I think we're going to need these," she said.

16
00:01:02.972 --> 00:01:06.435
Soon, everyone was in the spirit, helping to decorate the tree.

17
00:01:06.455 --> 00:01:09.858
"It looks beautiful!"

18
00:01:10.198 --> 00:01:10.718
said Ella.

19
00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:19.005
"Yes, I agree," Grandma said, "but I think it's missing something extra special."

20
00:01:19.025 --> 00:01:21.587
"Like what, Grandma?"

21
00:01:22.088 --> 00:01:22.608
asked Ella.

22
00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:29.253
"Well, I've got some old ornaments, from when I was a little girl.

23
00:01:30.154 --> 00:01:34.785
I've been saving them to share with you, and I think the time has come."

24
00:01:36.086 --> 00:01:38.587
Then she brought out a very old-looking box.

25
00:01:38.607 --> 00:01:43.130
"In here are my treasures from Christmas past.

26
00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:47.132
I have a story to tell about each ornament."

27
00:01:49.173 --> 00:01:52.315
Everyone excitedly gathered around Grandma as she began.

28
00:01:52.335 --> 00:02:01.740
"I remember the first time I walked into my hometown department store during Christmastime.

29
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:09.684
I was amazed at the beautiful display trees, all different sizes and colors, all brightly lit.

30
00:02:11.284 --> 00:02:14.486
I felt as if I were in a magical fairyland.

31
00:02:15.886 --> 00:02:20.208
My mother asked me to help her pick out some ornaments for our tree.

32
00:02:21.889 --> 00:02:26.611
I picked out these," said Grandma as she held up two golden balls.

33
00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:29.292
She twirled them between her fingers.

34
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.422
"I still love the way they sparkle."

35
00:02:33.442 --> 00:02:39.805
"They look like little twinkling stars," said Ella admiringly.

36
00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:46.169
"And here's my sweet little angel," said Grandma, reaching into the box.

37
00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.672
"My grandfather gave me this one Christmas.

38
00:02:51.912 --> 00:02:55.574
I thought it was the most beautiful thing I'd ever seen.

39
00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:58.196
See her little wings?

40
00:02:59.792 --> 00:03:02.254
I asked my grandfather if she could fly.

41
00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:07.978
He said, 'Yes, but only at night when we're asleep.'"

42
00:03:08.778 --> 00:03:09.679
Grandma chuckled.

43
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.164
"So I would sneak downstairs in the middle of the night, trying to catch her flying.

44
00:03:18.705 --> 00:03:23.848
I never did see her flying, but sometimes in my dreams I did!"

45
00:03:25.069 --> 00:03:25.790
Ella laughed.

46
00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.692
"So you did see her fly!

47
00:03:29.192 --> 00:03:30.153
What's next?"

48
00:03:32.094 --> 00:03:37.477
"Now this one Grandma held up a blue dog with a bone in its mouth.

49
00:03:37.497 --> 00:03:41.259
"My favorite teacher gave me this.

50
00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.301
She was always making things and giving them to her students.

51
00:03:47.762 --> 00:03:54.806
Look at the way she painted the dog's face, and on the back, she painted her name, Mrs.

52
00:03:54.886 --> 00:03:57.007
Beatty, and the year, 1944."

53
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:01.861
Ella looked thoughtful.

54
00:04:01.881 --> 00:04:06.124
"Your ornaments really are treasures, Grandma.

55
00:04:07.225 --> 00:04:08.786
How can you give them up?"

56
00:04:08.806 --> 00:04:14.630
"Because I know you will treasure them as much as I do.

57
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.692
Now this is the last ornament.

58
00:04:19.073 --> 00:04:21.714
I made this when I was in kindergarten.

59
00:04:24.056 --> 00:04:33.401
I remember how carefully I made it, gluing the wooden sticks together, letting the glue dry, then painting

60
00:04:33.461 --> 00:04:34.822
the whole thing white.

61
00:04:36.002 --> 00:04:39.424
It's held up pretty well all these years, I must say."

62
00:04:40.564 --> 00:04:43.625
Grandma held the snowflake ornament in front of the window.

63
00:04:44.886 --> 00:04:46.867
Snow was falling gently outside.

64
00:04:49.228 --> 00:04:50.548
Ella suddenly spoke up.

65
00:04:51.989 --> 00:04:53.149
"I have an idea!

66
00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.611
Why don't we make our own ornaments?"

67
00:04:57.971 --> 00:05:00.928
"That's a wonderful idea, Ella," said Dad.

68
00:05:00.948 --> 00:05:03.489
"But how are we going to make them?"

69
00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:10.071
"I know a recipe for making clay ornaments," said Grandma.

70
00:05:10.091 --> 00:05:14.832
"All we need is some flour, salt, and water.

71
00:05:16.072 --> 00:05:20.754
Then we cut the clay into shapes, bake our ornaments, and paint them."

72
00:05:22.714 --> 00:05:24.915
So everyone got busy making ornaments.

73
00:05:26.235 --> 00:05:32.361
Dad made a car, Mom made a shoe, Danny made a football, and Grandma made a gingerbread man.

74
00:05:33.721 --> 00:05:37.883
Ella took the longest, but when she was finished, she surprised everyone.

75
00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:46.765
"This is for you, Grandma," said Ella, "because you gave us your special ornaments."

76
00:05:47.826 --> 00:05:53.627
Ella made a snowflake with wings, put gold sparkles on it, and on the back, she had painted

77
00:05:53.647 --> 00:05:54.628
"Ella 2008."

78
00:05:57.184 --> 00:05:58.965
Grandma was moved to tears.

79
00:06:01.007 --> 00:06:06.991
"Ella, this is the most beautiful Christmas ornament I've ever had.

80
00:06:08.232 --> 00:06:10.514
I will treasure it forever."

81
00:06:11.855 --> 00:06:13.816
Ella gave Grandma a big hug.

82
00:06:13.836 --> 00:06:17.579
"And we will always treasure yours."
